1.Download any free APK file (for example, a simple calculator app) and install it on your Android emulator using Android Studio's Device Manager.
Answer :
>>Download and install an APK
-Download a free Calculator APK from a trusted APK website.
-Open Android Studio → Tools → Device Manager.
-Start an Android Virtual Device (AVD).
-Wait for the emulator to boot.
-Drag and drop the downloaded .apk file onto the running emulator.
-The APK will install automatically.
-Open the App Drawer and verify that the Calculator app is installed.
-Launch the app and check that it opens successfully.



2.Open the installed app on your emulator, rotate the device from portrait to landscape and back, and note any UI issues or layout problems that appear.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Use the emulator's rotate button to change orientation and take screenshots if you spot any glitches.</em>
Answer :
The installed app was opened on the Android Emulator and tested in both portrait and landscape orientations. The emulator’s Rotate button was used to change the screen orientation.

In portrait mode, the app displayed normally, with all buttons, text fields, and other UI elements properly aligned. After rotating to landscape mode, the layout adjusted to the wider screen without major issues. The text and buttons remained visible and usable. Rotating back to portrait mode also worked correctly.

Result: No major UI glitches or layout problems were observed during the orientation change. The app remained functional and displayed correctly in both orientations. Screenshots were taken for reference.


